3. How do you prevent race conditions in concurrent code?

Use synchronized blocks or Lock.
Use atomic classes (AtomicInteger, AtomicReference).
Use immutable objects wherever possible.
Avoid shared mutable state between threads.

-----
4. What is the difference between wait(), notify(), and notifyAll()?

wait() — releases lock and waits.
notify() — wakes one waiting thread.
notifyAll() — wakes all waiting threads.

-----
5. What’s a volatile variable and when should you use it?

Ensures visibility (not atomicity) of variable changes across threads.
Prevents CPU-level caching of variable values.

-----
6. Difference between ConcurrentHashMap and HashMap.

| Feature           | HashMap                | ConcurrentHashMap                   |
| ----------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Thread-Safe       | ❌                      | ✅                                   |
| Locking Mechanism | None                   | Fine-grained locking (bucket level) |
| Null Keys/Values  | Allowed                | Not allowed                         |
| Performance       | Fast (single-threaded) | Efficient in concurrent scenarios   |


